WEBVTT

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:09.480
<i>His subordinate, Ebitani, 
flies out of control!</i>

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.110
<b>Terminated!</b>

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.360
<b>Psst...</b>

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:14.360
<i>Ebitani's out!</i>

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:16.490
<i>With only a single strike!</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.250
<i>Tonegawa is hit, as well, 
with a pay reduction!</i>

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:23.500
<i>Reduction!</i>

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:28.070
<i>This man's pay? Reduced!</i>

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:35.010
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.670
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:43.020
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.710
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.610
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:59.620
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:10.170
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:10.170
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.550
<i>Looking ahead to 
Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors,</i>

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.750
<i>the cornerstone of the event, 
the </i>Espoir<i>, where it will be held,</i>

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:39.560
Luxury Liner
Espoir

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:39.560
<b>Restricted Rock-Paper-Scissors</b>

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:39.560
<b>Diabolical Game Day Notes</b>

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:39.560
<i>has been approved by Hyoudou!</i>

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:44.010
Diabolical Gambling Cruise 
Approved by the President

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:44.010
<i>The project is progressing smoothly!</i>

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.270
Design Meeting
Rock-Paper-Scissors Cards
Holster
Player

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.930
For the designs of these items,

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:50.420
we need to settle on our choices within a week,

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.060
<i>Agenda 07
</i><b>Proliferation</b>

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.150
at the least, of our first rehearsal day.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:56.150
<b>Players' Lives</b>

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.540
The loss of each one brings 
the player closer to losing,

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.890
which is a bit like dying, in this case...

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.660
So how about heart marks?

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.340
You mean like their life is 
literally being chipped away?

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.670
But... the players are going to be 
starting with three marks, right?

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.740
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.800
Wouldn't that make it seem like 
some matchmaking game?

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.430
What about cash bills?

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.970
Oh, that's realistic.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.490
A bit crass, though.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:32.060
Why not take the simple 
approach and just use stars?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.070
I get it. So as you lose, the stars 
that represent your hopes die out.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:41.320
It's a bit cliché, 
but it makes the most sense.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.320
<b>Rock-Paper-Scissors Cards</b>

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:47.660
Since it's rock-paper-scissors, I think 
the emphasis should be on readability.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:53.300
You mean having pictures of actual 
rocks, paper, and scissors?

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.790
That seems like it'd be harder 
to understand, honestly.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:57.800
I used the the male symbol for rock,

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.260
the female symbol for paper,

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:02.170
and the two linked together as scissors.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.330
I wanted to put an air of fun into it.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.560
It's incomprehensible!

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:12.940
We need something simple that can 
also put the pressure on our players.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:18.210
A type of psychological intensity beneath 
a veneer of play. An air of menace.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:20.200
That's the kind of design we want.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.080
Right.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.700
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:27.700
So, my idea for a design...

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.620
is this.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.580
Th-That's...

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:34.600
An X-ray?

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.970
Rock. Scissors. Paper.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.880
Using an X-ray motif for the designs 
gives them a hint of eeriness.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:46.510
Now that's a bright idea. Approved.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.510
Thank you, sir!

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.530
<i>The design motif for the cards is selected!</i>

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.520
<i>Now things are really moving toward 
the opening of Restricted RPS!</i>

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.520
<i>It's kick-off!</i>

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:04.780
About the matter we discussed the other day...

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.680
<i>The team is united in 
pursuit of a single goal!</i>

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.370
<i>To make a game! The holding 
of their diabolical diversion!</i>

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:19.880
<i>However, as the pressure piles on...</i>

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.880
Why the hell do we need 
X-rays of <i>your</i> hand?!

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:25.090
S-S-Sorry, sir!

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.590
Get a designer!

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.840
R-Right!

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.050
Tonegawa-sensei, when will 
you be inspecting the venue?

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:33.350
At the end of next week!

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:37.420
Tonegawa-sensei, what company should 
we approach for the holsters?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:40.340
One of the factories that 
work for us, obviously!

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.980
Tonegawa-sensei, what about 
lunch on the day of the event?

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.110
Unnecessary!

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:48.880
<i>Damn it all...</i>

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.890
<i>None of these fools has 
a speck of initiative.</i>

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:54.340
<i>Can't they do anything without being told?</i>

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:58.120
<i>What the hell would they do 
if something happened to me?</i>

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:00.630
Tonegawa-san!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.460
What now?!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.960
<b>Psst...</b>

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.780
It's Kawasaki-kun...

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:09.970
<b>Psst... Psst....</b>

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.970
H-He has a really high fever!

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.740
I-I'll take him to the break room!

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:17.160
Fool! Get him to a hospital!

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:18.530
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:23.550
<i>Tonegawa feels the fainest touch of dread...</i>

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:26.240
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:30.090
<i>He couldn't even manage his own health.</i>

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.140
<i>It's been an hour...</i>

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:37.000
Well, how is he?

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.000
W-Well...

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:44.490
It seems Kawasaki-kun... has the flu.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.010
<b>Psst...</b>

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.010
<i>His dread was justified!</i>

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.010
<b>Psst... Psst....</b>

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.510
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:51.930
<i>Chills run down their spines.</i>

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.760
<i>One thought crosses Tonegawa's mind:</i>

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.520
<b>Proliferation</b>

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:58.520
<i>The proliferation of the disease!</i>

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:01.770
Wh-What should we do, Tonegawa-san?!

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:04.650
There's nothing else to do.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.900
We have to go get them...

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.150
Go where?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.640
Get what?

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:15.780
Our flu shots. Right now!

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:22.040
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:22.040
<i>It was already the middle of winter!</i>

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.040
<b>Teiai Clinic
Now Taking Appointments
Monday - Friday  9:30-12:30
14:00-18:30</b>

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.800
<i>But there is resistance from Team Tonegawa!</i>

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.140
<i>And as of this day, it begins:</i>

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:50.610
<i>A full-force hygiene campaign 
under Tonegawa's direction!</i>

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.610
<b>Gargle!
Wash your hands!</b>

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:54.750
I've asked the president 
to avoid the meeting room

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.010
for the foreseeable future.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.620
<b>Gargle!
Wash your hands!</b>

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.290
Keep your masks on at all times.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:06.340
Listen up. The antibodies from immunization 
take one to two weeks to build up.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:09.130
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:09.130
Which means...

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.380
You must stay on your toes at all times.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:15.410
<b>Psst...</b>

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:17.160
<i>It was as if they were waging war with a 
grim reaper by the name of "influenza"...</i>

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:20.890
<i>A defensive front from which 
no retreat could be tolerated!</i>

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.890
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.150
Stretch out those necks!

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.400
Make sure it gets down into your throat!

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:41.160
Okay, that's plenty of suds. 
Should be enough...

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:44.710
No!

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.510
Tonegawa-sensei?

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:49.430
Not good enough at all.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:49.960
Sir...?

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.130
<b>Bubble...</b>

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:58.300
Washing your hands is about more 
than just lathering up some suds

00:08:56.530 --> 00:09:00.970
<b>Bubble...</b>

00:08:58.300 --> 00:08:59.890
and rinsing them off with water.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:05.480
You get between your fingers, 
under your nails...

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.480
<b>Bubble... Bubble...</b>

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:09.060
And don't stop at the hand.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.480
Take it to the limit!

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:14.610
<b>Bubble...</b>

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.610
Down the elbow.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.810
T-To the elbow, sir?

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:24.070
<i>They are prepared to wage 
vicious war against the reaper.</i>

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:25.860
<i>Influenza is on the march!</i>

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:28.750
<i>They will defend with the shield 
of disinfectant soap</i>

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.380
<i>and the sword known as gargling!</i>

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:38.140
Even with all this, we're still 
only looking at half-half odds.

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:41.570
Don't underestimate the difference 
washing hands can make!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.640
<b>Three Days Later...</b>

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.650
Excuse me...

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.520
Tonegawa-sensei?

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:56.480
What is it, Saemon?

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.160
Well, sir... it's been three days.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.660
Is it all right if we take the masks off?

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.490
Fool! That's a terrible id—

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:07.700
They're all fogged up!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.040
Fog?

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:12.420
My sunglasses! Because of 
this mask and the humidity!

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:18.930
It's like I'm trapped deep in some 
fog, nothing but hazy darkness.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:22.430
I can't get any work done like this!

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.200
Tonegawa-sensei, I'm fogged up, too!

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.110
Me, too!

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:29.560
Please, sir!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:34.070
We've been gargling and washing our 
hands thoroughly, like you said!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.860
And we've been staying at 
home when not at work.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.580
No one else has gotten sick, either!

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:46.070
All right. I'll allow it.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:54.030
<i>Well, no one has gotten sick since Kawasaki.</i>

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:57.970
<i>There's probably no need 
to be so cautious anym—</i>

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.180
Tonegawa-san?!

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.740
<i>It slips from Tonegawa's throat! 
The first cough!</i>

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:10.060
<b>Psst...</b>

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:10.060
<b>Cough</b>

00:11:13.010 --> 00:11:16.920
<i>It's a sign from the reaper!</i>

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.040
Damn it!

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:30.410
Gonda-san!

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.500
How is Tonegawa-sensei?

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:36.090
He's out.

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:38.010
Tonegawa-san...

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.970
has come down with the flu.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.920
He's recuperating at home.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:48.720
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.050
Oh, no...

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:48.720
How are we going to get anything 
done on the project without him?

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.380
We can't, that's how!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:53.230
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:51.950
It can't be done!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.230
It's impossible!

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:59.990
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.310
Maybe we could ask President Hyoudou?

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:59.990
That's crazy! We'd just end up like Ebitani.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:04.470
We'll have to put the project 
on hiatus until he's back...

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:09.870
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:07.830
But the day of the rehearsal is already set.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.880
Then what should we do?!

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:12.870
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.100
What should we do?

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:12.870
I don't know!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.440
Without any direction...

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:16.380
Oh, no.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:20.290
Gonda-san?

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:24.090
You young punks need to settle down!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:32.600
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:28.100 --> 00:12:32.600
Tonegawa-san gets sick, 
and you all start whining?

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:37.560
He's not your mother, damn it!

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.110
<b>Psst...</b>

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.360
You don't need to worry. I can...

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:43.700
No...

00:12:44.440 --> 00:12:47.080
I'm going to stand in for Tonegawa-san!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.370
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:50.370
<b>Psst...</b>

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.620
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:54.870
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:58.960
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.610
U-Um...

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:01.030
Are you gonna be okay?

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:02.630
O-Of course I will!

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:04.180
Leave it to me!

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:06.410
I can— I'll handle it!

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:09.350
<i>That's right. He entrusted this to me.</i>

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:13.850
Gonda... Until I get back,

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:18.360
you have to stand in for me.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.250
M-Me, sir?!

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.360
That's right.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.670
S-Sir, I don't think I have what it takes...

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.520
You've got seniority. I'm counting on you.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:31.120
T-Tonegawa-san!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:37.870
<i>I have to live up...</i>

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:41.210
<i>to his expectations!</i>

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:45.720
<i>And so, with a sudden reshuffling,</i>

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:49.770
<i>the unprecedented Gonda 
administration begins!</i>

00:13:57.650 --> 00:13:59.610
Um, Gonda-san...

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:03.280
Did you... always smoke?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.530
I know you're standing 
in for Tonegawa-sensei,

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:14.160
but do you really need to take it that far?

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:17.160
G-Good point.

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.050
Excuse me, Gonda-san.

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:26.420
About the rock-paper-scissors cards... 
How many sets should we order?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:30.430
W-Well, that's... uh...

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:35.690
<i>The worst case scenario is not having enough.</i>

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:37.930
<i>So let's lean toward too many...</i>

00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:40.310
T-Ten thousand.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:41.470
H-Huh?!

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:44.310
N-no, never mind! Nine thousand! 
Nine thousand sets!

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:47.060
U-Understood. Nine thousand, then.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:50.550
Gonda-san!

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:54.490
About the cash holsters the 
debtors will be using...

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:55.950
Y-Yeah?

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:59.770
Should they be made out of cloth or leather?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.170
L-Leather!

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.860
What type of leather should we use?!

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:08.840
Uh... er... cattle!

00:15:09.190 --> 00:15:11.470
What about the color, sir?!

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.770
B-B-Brown... maybe?

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.480
Brown?! Understood!

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:22.230
W-Wait!

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:23.690
Yes?!

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.370
Perhaps... b-black?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:27.480
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:27.480
Which one, sir?

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:30.990
W-We'll go with black!

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.620
Right! Black it is, then.

00:15:39.240 --> 00:15:41.120
You think he's gonna be okay?

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:43.000
What do you mean?

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:45.880
<b>Bubble... Bubble...</b>

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:45.880
I'm talking about Gonda-san.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:49.260
Well, he is the oldest among us.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:16:01.520
<b>Bubble... Bubble...</b>

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.490
It's kind of obvious how anxious he is...

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:57.570
And the way he's desperate to keep us 
from noticing just makes me more anxious.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:16:01.520
Still, he's the one who said he'd handle it.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:07.930
<i>And yet, in spite of Saemon-saburou's 
concerns, for all the bumps in the road,</i>

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:11.530
<i>Team Gonda is, at very least, 
operational for now.</i>

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.650
<b>Splash!</b>

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:15.410
<i>However, two days later...</i>

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.550
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:23.040
Gonda-san... Maybe you 
should go to the hospital.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.180
I'm fine!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:28.500
It's just a slight fever and aching 
in every single one of my joints.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:29.890
No problem here!

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.680
Th-That sounds like...

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:38.210
<i>The reaper rears his head again with no mercy!</i>

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.180
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.080
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:42.430
He definitely has the flu.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:44.340
Wh-What do we do?!

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:45.910
What <i>can</i> we do?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:48.250
He should probably go home.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.690
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:57.950
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:16:50.050 --> 00:16:53.670
You remember what Tonegawa-sensei 
said about underestimating the flu.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:57.950
I guess I just wasn't cut out for it...

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:06.230
A pitiful, unremarkable guy like 
me, trying to act as leader.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:11.710
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:11.710
And to top it off, I get the flu!

00:17:13.540 --> 00:17:14.720
I'm a damn scarecrow...

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:22.720
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.740
No better than a scarecrow!

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:20.390
N-No, I wouldn't say that...

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:22.720
I knew the truth all along.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.550
The fact that I'm still just 
a man in black at my age

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:31.480
proves that I have no hope 
of moving up in the ranks.

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.610
I never thought it'd be easy.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:39.840
I'm just fully aware of how powerless 
people... no, how powerless I am.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.590
That's not what we were talking about.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:45.380
But I got what I had coming.

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.260
Thinking back, for the past 50 years,

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:55.050
I've run from responsibility whenever I could.

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.860
I always chose the easy, safe position.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.190
I chose safety...

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:09.930
And the result?

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:13.940
You're so irresponsible! 
Always taking the easy way out!

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.100
Always choosing the safest option!

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:22.230
It's a miracle I got into Teiai and 
managed to survive here this long...

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:27.090
That's why I'm ranked where I am now.

00:18:27.780 --> 00:18:30.970
I'm not the kind of guy who should 
have authority over others.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:36.460
I'm not... but he...

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:39.880
He asked me to be the leader!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:42.180
Tonegawa-san did!

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:46.290
I'm begging you guys! Let me finish the job!

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.350
I want to live up to his hopes!

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.230
If I give up now,

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:57.490
I'll never be able to live with myself!

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:12.750
There's no time to rest, you know!

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.760
Gonda-san, look here.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.950
Thanks to you, they're ready.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.260
Our diabolical holsters!

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.890
D-Doushita-kun...

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:30.960
We're counting on you until 
Tonegawa-sensei gets back, Leader.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.020
L-Leader?!

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:34.200
That's right, Leader!

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:36.520
This is no time to talk about feeling sick!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.390
We've still got a ton of work to do!

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:43.030
Let's give Tonegawa-sensei a 
big surprise when he gets back!

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.910
I bet he'll be really impressed!

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:48.290
And he'll be glad he left 
you in charge, Gonda-san!

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.100
You guys...

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.920
You're kind of cool right now, Gonda-san.

00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.670
All right! Let's do this!

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:00.910
Yeah!

00:20:00.910 --> 00:20:02.870
<i>The sentiment spreads!</i>

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.860
<i>Motivation is transmitted 
throughout all of Team Gonda!</i>

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:08.680
<i>They are united!</i>

00:20:09.620 --> 00:20:11.210
<i>Two days later...</i>

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:17.440
<i>Tonegawa returns!</i>

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.950
<i>Gonda...</i>

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:22.520
<i>I would've never considered 
him leadership material,</i>

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:25.190
<i>but I chose to put him in that position.</i>

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:28.990
<i>Sometimes giving someone
responsibility motivates them...</i>

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.990
<i>And seeing someone unreliable 
in a position of authority</i>

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:35.300
<i>should motivate the rest of the team.</i>

00:20:35.720 --> 00:20:39.330
<i>It should help them grow out of being 
a bunch of drones who wait for orders!</i>

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.430
Good mor—

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:48.010
<i>Proliferation! Pandemic!</i>

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.730
<i>It spread among them...</i>

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:52.790
What's wrong with you all?!

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.610
Tonegawa-san... I did... it...

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.510
<i>Gonda's passion and his virus!</i>

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:10.660
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer,</i>

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:14.990
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:19.590
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:56.950
Next time: "Shrimp."

00:22:55.700 --> 00:23:00.500
<b>Shrimp</b>
